 "protocol": {
  "summary": "Costal cartilage with rib part (perichondrium status: see paper, Fig 1 cross-section shown without perichondrium), moulded fixation; rib end clamped and cartilage loaded as cantilever (force at sternal end, max 4 N) in anterior (B1), superior (B2), posterior (B3), inferior (B4) directions -> bending moduli from elliptical cross-section beam theory; torsion via force couple (max 5 N, 175 Nmm) in two directions (GT1, GT2); tension along the cartilage axis to 50 N at 1.3e-3 /s -> secant modulus between 20 and 40 N. Each test 3 times, 2nd and 3rd used. Samples refrigerated at 5-7 C.",
  "how_to_simulate": [
   "Model the costal cartilage as a cantilever fixed at the rib with elliptical cross-section a x b and free length l (Table 2)",
   "Apply the small tip force (<=4 N bending, <=175 Nmm torsion, <=50 N tension) in the stated direction",
   "Back-calculate modulus with beam theory as the authors did, or compare tip deflection/twist"
  ],
  "subject_model": null,
  "notes": ""
 },
